(R WORKSHOP: PRACTICAL CURRICULUM) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Programme: Applied R for Statistical Teaching, Research and Reproducible Analysis) Tj
T* (Audience: Statistics lecturers and academic staff who need to teach, analyse and report with) Tj
T* (  R) Tj
T* (Format: Seven guided sessions, three hours each, supported by reference workbooks and) Tj
T* (  independent capstone work) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1. Curriculum promise) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (This is not a race through seven dense manuals. The workshop uses the full workbooks as a) Tj
T* (  lasting reference handbook, while the live sessions focus on the essential tasks) Tj
T* (  participants need in order to build one coherent analysis.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The workshop will briefly revisit statistical theory where necessary to connect equations,) Tj
T* (  assumptions and interpretation to their implementation in R. It will not attempt to) Tj
T* (  reteach an entire statistics degree, nor will it become a machine-learning or Shiny) Tj
T* (  course.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2. Delivery model) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Each workbook section should be labelled in the teaching copy as one of the following.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Label  Meaning  Live-session expectation) Tj
T* (Core workshop activity  Essential skill or concept needed for the daily deliverable and) Tj
T* (  capstone  Teach and practise during the three-hour session) Tj
T* (Optional demonstration  Useful extension if the group is fast or the facilitator wants to) Tj
T* (  show breadth  Demonstrate briefly or skip) Tj
T* (Reference or take-home material  Valuable background, extra methods or fuller explanations) Tj
T* (  Assign for independent study) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (A realistic three-hour session should include approximately:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Segment  Time  Purpose) Tj
T* (Opening and recap  10 minutes  Reconnect with the anchor dataset and prior deliverable) Tj
T* (Concept bridge  25 minutes  Explain the statistical or reproducibility idea) Tj
T* (Guided coding  60 minutes  Work through the core R workflow) Tj
T* (Participant practice  45 minutes  Apply the workflow to the anchor dataset) Tj
T* (Interpretation and reporting  25 minutes  Translate outputs into statistical language) Tj
T* (Evidence log and capstone update  15 minutes  Save artefacts and plan next steps) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3. Anchor dataset and capstone thread) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Use one anchor dataset from Day 2 through Day 7. Demonstration datasets may still appear,) Tj
T* (  but they must be labelled as demonstration datasets and should not replace the capstone) Tj
T* (  thread.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Day  Capstone progress) Tj
T* (Day 1  Confirm software setup and complete a baseline task) Tj
T* (Day 2  Select a research question, clean the anchor dataset and document variables) Tj
T* (Day 3  Produce exploratory figures and write initial observations) Tj
T* (Day 4  Perform one inferential analysis linked to the research question) Tj
T* (Page 1 of 7) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
