(Day 5  Fit and diagnose the principal statistical model) Tj
T* (Day 6  Recreate or examine part of the model from its equation) Tj
T* (Day 7  Integrate, render, peer-review and present the report) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (By the start of Day 7, every participant should already have a cleaned dataset, a defined) Tj
T* (  research question, at least two visualisations, one inferential result or model and draft) Tj
T* (  interpretations.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (4. Assessment and evidence) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Assessment is evidence-based and practical. Participants maintain a workshop evidence log) Tj
T* (  with four checks: evidence produced, participant check, peer check and capstone update.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The same short task should be attempted on Day 1 and repeated on Day 7 with an equivalent) Tj
T* (  dataset:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1. Import a small dataset.) Tj
T* (2. Identify missing or invalid values.) Tj
T* (3. Produce one numerical summary and one labelled plot.) Tj
T* (4. Write three sentences interpreting the result for a non-technical reader.) Tj
T* (5. Save the script, output and interpretation in the project folder.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (5. Curriculum at a glance) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Day  Session title  Core live focus  Daily deliverable  Capstone link) Tj
T* (1  Getting Comfortable with R  RStudio projects, assignment, vectors, indexing, missing) Tj
T* (  values, data frames, descriptive statistics and reading error messages  Working R project) Tj
T* (  and first script  Baseline task and software readiness) Tj
T* (2  Importing, Cleaning and Preparing Data  Import, inspect, flag invalid values, standardise) Tj
T* (  categories, handle missingness, remove duplicates, export clean data  Clean anchor) Tj
T* (  dataset, data-quality report and data dictionary  Research question, cleaned data and) Tj
T* (  variable documentation) Tj
T* (3  Exploratory Data Analysis and Statistical Graphics  Question-led plot choice, bar charts,) Tj
T* (  histograms, box plots, scatter plots, labels, themes, export and interpretation  Three) Tj
T* (  interpreted graphics  Initial visual evidence for the capstone) Tj
T* (4  Probability, Sampling, Simulation and Inference  d/p/q/r functions, set.seed\(\), one) Tj
T* (  simulation, one CLT demonstration, one confidence interval, test selection and plain-) Tj
T* (  language reporting  Inference or simulation notebook  One inferential answer to the) Tj
T* (  capstone question) Tj
T* (5  Regression, ANOVA and Generalised Linear Models  Formula notation, multiple linear) Tj
T* (  regression, categorical predictors, one interaction, diagnostics, one-way ANOVA and) Tj
T* (  reporting  Diagnosed model report  Principal model for the capstone) Tj
T* (6  Coding Statistical Models from Their Equations  Matrix operations, design matrices, OLS) Tj
T* (  derivation, custom function, validation against lm\(\) and one numerical failure mode) Tj
T* (  Equation-based implementation  Mathematical audit of part of the model) Tj
T* (7  Reproducible Research and Capstone Presentation  Project organisation, Quarto basics,) Tj
T* (  code-cell options, multi-format rendering, clean-session checks, peer review and) Tj
T* (  presentations  Reproducible final report  Integrated capstone report and presentation) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (6. Day-by-day teaching plan) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Day 1: Getting Comfortable with R) Tj
T* (Page 2 of 7) Tj
ET
endstream
